## Instructions for Managing Subagents\
\
(1) Group deltas together by subject and fix requirement similarities \
\
*2) Sequence the implementation of the groups\
\
(4) Assign subagents to the group or groups that are most applicable to their areas of expertise\
\
(5) Decide how many copies of each subagent is necessary to efficiently and effectively perform the tasks necessary to fix the deltas in that group\
\
(6) Sequence the deployment so the right subagents are deployed when their assigned group or groups are next in the sequence.\
\
(7) Begin creating the plan.\
\
        (A) Call you coordinator and managing subagents who will be deployed the duration of the planning process.\
\
        (B) Deploy the subagents assigned to the first group\
\
       (C) Begin planning for the first group,\
\
       (D) When planning is complete, dismiss the subagents for that group \
\
       (E) Call the subagents for the next group.\
\
      (F) Begin planning fixes for the second group\
\
      (G) Continue this process until the plan is complete.\
\
\
The plan should be highly specific and include two documents:\
\
(1) The first document identifies the subagents who should be involved in the actual building process and it should resemble Users/masterrabbit/Software/Syxx/SUBAGENT_DEPLOYMENT_PLAN.md in terms of content, detail granularity, etc.\
\
(2) The second documen should be the build plan itself, and it should look like /Users/masterrabbit/Software/Syxx/UNIFIED_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md iin terms of content and detail granularity.\
\
The finished product should be a highly specific document with granular details about what is being implemented to fix each delta, which subagents get deployed when, etc.\
\
In short, you\'92re not building the implementation plan the subagents with their specialized knowledge are building the plan at your direction.\
\
